-- title:
--   Counting ∞-side zeros via the q-order drop under reduction
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$; fix $\mathrm{data}$, consisting of a monic $\Phi\in\mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ vanishing at $(j,j_q)$, together with the hypothesis $h_{Kr}$ that its reduction modulo $q$ is $(C(X)^q-X)\,(C(X)-X^q)$, and the hypotheses $h_\alpha,h_\beta$ that the ring homomorphisms underlying the bar Hecke maps $\alpha,\beta$ at level $1$ and prime $q$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ are integral. Let $P$ be a `PlaceSpecialization` for these data, i.e. a map $\mathrm{sp}$ from places of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(X_0(1))$-type function field `modularFunctionFieldBar 1` to places of the corresponding field over $k$ together with a map on degree-zero divisor classes, subject to the compatibility axioms of that structure. Let $x$ be a nonzero element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` (a subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$) lying in the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$ and $t_\infty=j_q/j^{\,1\cdot q}$. Then there are $c\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$, and a finite set $S$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ such that: $c\neq 0$; the image of $y$ under the coefficientwise inclusion $A\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$ equals $c\cdot x$ as Laurent series; the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $A\to A/\mathfrak m_A$ is nonzero; $W\in S$ holds exactly when $P.\mathrm{IsInftySide}\,W$ (that is, $W$ satisfies $P$'s predicate `IsCuspidal` and there is $\tau\in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,\tau=1$ and $t_\infty$ in the valuation subring of $W$ with residue the image of $\tau$), $W\neq$ `cuspInftyBar (1 * q)`, and $\mathrm{ord}_W(x)\neq 0$; and $\sum_{W\in S}\mathrm{ord}_W(x)$ equals the Hahn-series order of the reduction of $y$ minus the order of $y$.
--
--   This is the counting form of the Tate uniformisation of the $\infty$-tube: the $\infty$-side places of the level-$q$ modular function field other than the cusp at infinity correspond to zeros in the open unit $\mathfrak q$-disc, whose total multiplicity is the Weierstrass degree of an $A$-integral $\mathfrak q$-expansion, namely the drop in order upon reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. It is used in the level-one prolongation-pair development, in the proofs of [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.cuspLawInfty`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.cuspLawInfty) and its one-sided variant.
